		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Announcement: Field3D library now available]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=14860#p14860"><![CDATA[
Field3D is an open source library for storing voxel data. It provides C++ classes that handle in-memory storage and a file format based on HDF5 that allows the C++ objects to be written to and read from disk.<br><br>The library is part of Imageworks' open source effort and was launched on Google Code a few weeks ago. The code base is available as of today via SVN (also through Google Code).<br><br>More information about the project can be found at: <a href="http://code.google.com/p/field3d/" class="postlink">http://code.google.com/p/field3d/</a><br><br>OpenSource at Imageworks: <a href="http://opensource.imageworks.com/" class="postlink">http://opensource.imageworks.com/</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5531">magnus.wrenninge</a> — Sat Aug 22, 2009 1:05 am</p><hr />
